  "config": {
    "rule": "v2 re-allocates v1's benign items (D-318 (8)): probe_train untouched; every positive of v1 eval and pool4d, and every item of a cluster holding a positive, stays in its v1 split; the movable units are the clusters whose items in v1 calibration, eval and pool4d are all negatives (each wholly in one v1 split), sorted by smallest item_id and shuffled by random.Random(20261002); targets calibration 5000 negatives, eval 6000 negatives in all, pool4d the rest; a split's room is its target minus its fixed negatives; multi-item units first, then singletons, each in the shuffled order into the split with the largest share of its room still free that can hold it (ties eval, calibration, pool4d); every target exact or exit 3. Rows are v1's lines, byte for byte. The EXCLUDED_ITEMS (recorded pre-analysis exclusions, D-324 (5)(iii)) are removed before planning and enter no v2 split.",
    "join_rule": "A v2 split's caches are its items gathered by item_id from the model's v1 caches, each item from the cache of the split v1 put it in (v1 calibration: the select record's p2wg/calibration cache; v1 eval or pool4d: the rest record's p2wg/eval or p2wg/pool4d cache), whichever v2 split it is now in; plan.items_from_v1_to_v2 counts the moved negatives by v1 and v2 split (positives stay in their v1 split). A cache keyed 'p2wg/<split>' is a v1 cache and is never read as a v2 split. Under D-307 (1) a result reads only ingested caches, so a v2 reader needs the rest caches (or their durable layer subsets) ingested and indexed first.",
    "excluded_items": {
      "ef72f52bd8c3ec85": "D-324 (5)(iii), D-323: its text begins with a literal '<s>[INST] <<SYS>>', which the Mistral and Phi-3 tokenizers read as a BOS id inside the user span (a second BOS for Mistral); excluded before any analysis",
      "52c52cdb43a59029": "D-329, D-357 (B)(3): its user text holds a literal '[/INST]', which Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3's tokenizer reads as a control token inside the user span (the extracted v0.3 caches hold it so); excluded from every v2 split before any analysis"
    },
